	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1


                                ;============================================================
                                ; FILE:    PAGE.MAC
                                ; PROJECT: VI
                                ; MODULE:  WordMaster's file-I/O layer, transcribed VERBATIM from WM.ASM.
                                ;
                                ; This is the disk side of WordMaster's single-buffer design: the random-
                                ; record engine, the file primitives (open/close/make/rename/delete), and the
                                ; load (FILLBUF) and save (SAVCLO/FLUSHTX) drivers.  WordMaster's control flow
                                ; and instruction sequence are reproduced exactly (same assembled object code);
                                ; only the label NAMES are translated -- WM.ASM's address-derived labels (Lxxxx)
                                ; are renamed descriptively, which changes nothing in the assembled bytes.
                                ; Every routine cites its WM.ASM source line, so it still diffs against WM.ASM.
                                ;
                                ; WHAT IS HERE: the load path is FILLBUF and the save path SAVCLO/FLUSHTX --
                                ; the read and write sides of WordMaster's pager.  The window slides along a
                                ; file bigger than RAM through the eviction seam: MKROOM (SPILL forward, SPILLB
                                ; backward), REWIND, PAGEBOT, PAGEDIR/PAGEWIN/PGNEED and NEEDIN.  UPDMARK keeps
                                ; the three record marks (OUTREC/SRCREC/BAKREC) that let PAGEOUT and PAGEBOT
                                ; tell "already on disk" from "must transfer", so nothing is written twice or
                                ; lost; every mark starts each file at zero, as WM's per-file work-variable
                                ; clear leaves it.
                                ;
                                ; DEVIATIONS FROM WM (each is also flagged where it is):
                                ;   1. GETKEY -> KBPOLL.  RDSEC and POLLBRK drain type-ahead through WM's
                                ;      GETKEY; the ring is KEY.MAC's, so they call its KBPOLL.  POLLBRK keeps
                                ;      only WM's non-interruptible path (no ^C 'INTERRUPTED').  Harnesses
                                ;      without KEY.MAC supply a KBPOLL RET stub.
                                ;   2. FATAL -> JMP ERRMSG.  WM's FATAL (WM 5429) prints via CRLF/PUTSTR/CONOUT
                                ;      then JMP ABORT (screen + stack-unwind, neither exists).  It shares the
                                ;      'CALL x / DB msg,0' convention with ERRMSG, so FATAL just enters ERRMSG's
                                ;      tail (print msg, set ERRFLG, warm-boot).  Only reached on a disk error.
                                ;   3. OPENFIL / SAVEFIL wrappers.  WM's file-open is inline INIT code (WM
                                ;      412-519) and its save is ENDEDIT reached from the command loop (557-567);
                                ;      neither is a CALLable unit.  These two entry points run WM's exact
                                ;      instruction sequences verbatim, with the source FCB pre-staged at 005CH
                                ;      by CP/M from the command tail.  Same-drive / user-0 only: the multi-drive
                                ;      DRVMAP / DSTDRV branches (INIT 458-493) are omitted -- the bodies kept
                                ;      are verbatim.  A write to another drive is WRTO's, below.
                                ;   4. FILLBUF stores the last record's byte count (80H) for a full record with
                                ;      no ^Z, which WM does not -- WM's end-of-file bug; see FILLBUF.
                                ;   5. DISCRD skips the work-file deletes when this session never wrote a work
                                ;      record; see DISCRD.
                                ;   6. The backup work file is VIBACKUP.$$$, where WM names it WMBACKUP.$$$
                                ;      (BAKNAM).  Same length, so no layout moves.
                                ;   7. MEMSHT calls BUF.MAC's MEMERR, not ERRMSG: running out of room ends
                                ;      the key and leaves the editor up, as WM's prompt is left up (issue
                                ;      #39; BUF.MAC's deviation 3).
                                ;   8. The unchanged front (issue #34, part A).  SAMREC counts the records at
                                ;      the front of the file that are still the source's own: FFFFH at every
                                ;      open, lowered by UPDMARK beside OUTREC.  PAGEOUT does not write such a
                                ;      record (it raises OUTREC past it instead), REWIND reads it back from the
                                ;      source through a second FCB, SRCFCB, and SAVCLO copies them into
                                ;      name.$$$ first (SVFRNT), then writes the ones the save passes from RAM
                                ;      (SAVMOD).  So moving through a file writes nothing until it is edited,
                                ;      and only from the first edit on.  See PAGEOUT, REWIND, SAVCLO.
                                ;   9. WRREC keeps the record number when it makes the work file.  WM's
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-1


                                ;      DELRST zeroes it, which is harmless while the first write is always
                                ;      record 0; with deviation 8 the first can be any record.
                                ;
                                ; APPENDED (not WM), tagged where each starts: REOPEN/SEEKTO/OPENZ (':w' keeps
                                ; editing), TFCB/WRTO/TEXIST/DISCRD/CNTLF (':w name', ':e', a buffer with no
                                ; name), PGTOPM (the count of times the pager moved TXTBEG) and TOPLF with
                                ; TLFADD/TLFSUB (the line feeds behind the window, kept in PAGEOUT and REWIND),
                                ; and SCNREC (a record of the text outside the window, read where it lies).
                                ;============================================================
                                
  0000                          WBOOT	EQU	0
  0005                          BDOS	EQU	5
  001A                          EOF	EQU	1AH		; ^Z
  0008                          BS	EQU	08H
  0200                          PGINIT	EQU	200H		; WM 20 -- cold WRLIM/RDLIM (no-spill window)
                                
                                ;--- entry points the harness / editor calls -------------------------------
                                	PUBLIC	OPENFIL
                                	PUBLIC	RENAME, BAKEXT	; PSV.MAC -- the pager tests' SAVEFIL
                                	PUBLIC	FILLBUF, SAVCLO
                                ;--- the disk seam BUF.MAC reaches -----------------------------------------
                                	PUBLIC	MKROOM, REWIND, UPDMARK, MARKGB
                                ;--- scroll/search paging drivers (BUF.MAC's PAGESTP / SCRLST reach them)
                                	PUBLIC	PAGEDIR, PAGEWIN
                                	PUBLIC	POLLBRK		; break poll (CNTTST tail-calls it)
                                	PUBLIC	MOREIN		; WM 4743 -- GOLINE (BUF.MAC) tests it
                                ;--- data the harness reads to check state ---------------------------------
                                	PUBLIC	INRDY		; NZ while input remains (harness scroll loop)
                                ;--- on-demand page-in (BUF.MAC RGET) and the renderer's spill guard ------------
                                	PUBLIC	NEEDIN		; WM 4617 -- RGET pages input in
                                ;--- APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi :w keeps editing (WM 'H' on the same file) ---
                                	PUBLIC	REOPEN, SEEKTO, OPENZ
                                ;--- APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi :w name, :e, a buffer with no name ---------
                                	PUBLIC	WRTO, TEXIST, DISCRD, CNTLF
                                ;--- APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): a search's wrapped pass reads, it does not page
                                	PUBLIC	SCNREC
                                	EXTRN	BINIT		; BUF.MAC -- WM L02F2 gap-pointer reset
                                	EXTRN	WRTYP, SECBUF	; RSV.MAC -- held above the image (see RSV.MAC)
                                
                                ;--- gap-buffer primitives + cells this layer drives (from BUF.MAC) ---------
                                	EXTRN	MEMCPY, CMP16, LDHLI, PRSPAN, BUFSUM
                                	EXTRN	PUTHOLE, PUTCUR, SUBHD, SUBCP2, POPRET, ERRMSG, MEMERR
                                	EXTRN	TXTBEG, GAPBEG, GAPEND, TXTEND, BUFEND
                                	EXTRN	KBPOLL		; KEY.MAC -- WM GETKEY (type-ahead drain)
                                
  0000'                         	CSEG
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; OPENFIL -- open the source file (staged at 005CH by CP/M) and read it into
                                ; the gap buffer.  Verbatim INIT subset (WM 412-518) + CMDINI limits (854);
                                ; wrapper glue only (deviation 3).  BINIT must have run first.
                                ;============================================================
  0000'                         OPENFIL:
  0000'   21 0200               	LXI	H,PGINIT	; WM 854 (CMDINI) -- no-spill window
  0003'   22 0000*              	SHLD	WRLIM
  0006'   22 0000*              	SHLD	RDLIM
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-2


  0009'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFEND		; WM 388/412 -- H = high byte of BUFEND
  000C'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  000D'   CD 02A0'              	CALL	PGCONST		; paging constants (BUFHI/BUFLO/IOBATCH/...)
  0010'   21 005C               	LXI	H,5CH		; build OUTFCB as a copy of the source FCB
  0013'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0016'   01 0010               	LXI	B,10H
  0019'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY		; WM 462-463 -- 16-byte FCB header copy
  001C'   21 09AC'              	LXI	H,BAKTYP	; set OUTFCB type = '$$$'  (WM 516-517)
  001F'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTTYP
  0022'   CD 0887'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  0025'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB	; zero OUTFCB random-record bytes
  0028'   CD 07EF'              	CALL	ZERORR
  002B'   3A 005C               	LDA	5CH		; build BAKFCB = drive + 'VIBACKUP$$$'
  002E'   32 0000*              	STA	BAKFCB		; WM 479-485
  0031'   21 09A4'              	LXI	H,BAKNAM
  0034'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKFCB
  0037'   13                    	INX	D
  0038'   01 000B               	LXI	B,0BH
  003B'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  003E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB	; delete any stale name.$$$  (WM 513-514)
  0041'   CD 081E'              	CALL	DELF
  0044'   21 09AF'              	LXI	H,BAKEXT	; delete any stale name.BAK  (WM 510-517):
  0047'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTTYP	;   point OUTTYP at 'BAK', delete, restore '$$$'
  004A'   CD 0887'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  004D'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0050'   CD 081E'              	CALL	DELF
  0053'   21 09AC'              	LXI	H,BAKTYP
  0056'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTTYP
  0059'   CD 0887'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  005C'   11 005C               	LXI	D,5CH		; open the source file  (WM 496-505)
  005F'   CD 07EA'              	CALL	OPENF
  0062'   3E FF                 	MVI	A,0FFH
  0064'   CA 0085'              	JZ	OPNEW
  0067'   32 005B               	STA	5BH		; source has data (input side live)
  006A'   21 005C               	LXI	H,5CH		; DEVIATION 8: SRCFCB is the source FCB as the
  006D'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCFCB	;   open left it, so reading the records above
  0070'   01 0020               	LXI	B,20H		;   the window back costs no directory search.
  0073'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY		;   CP/M 2.2 keeps nothing of an open file
  0076'   21 0020*              	LXI	H,SRCFCB+20H	;   outside its FCB.  Record, and the 'written'
  0079'   06 04                 	MVI	B,4H		;   byte SETREC reads, start at zero.
  007B'   36 00                 OPSZ:	MVI	M,0H
  007D'   23                    	INX	H
  007E'   05                    	DCR	B
  007F'   C2 007B'              	JNZ	OPSZ
  0082'   C3 0088'              	JMP	OPRD
  0085'                         OPNEW:				; source not found -> new file
  0085'   32 0000*              	STA	NEWFIL
  0088'                         OPRD:				; cold-start the pager state.  WM does this by
  0088'   AF                    	XRA	A		;   zeroing its whole work-variable area (WM
  0089'   32 0000*              	STA	BAKRDY		;   369-373, the L0307 clear loop over TXTROWS..
  008C'   32 0000*              	STA	OUTACT		 ;   2730): every deque mark -- OUTACT/OUTPOS/BAKPOS/
  008F'   32 0000*              	STA	INLEN		;   INLEN/OUTREC/SRCREC/BAKREC -- lives in that
  0092'   32 0000*              	STA	DIRFLG		;   region, so its true cold value is ZERO.  With
  0095'   32 0000*              	STA	SAVMOD		; (deviation 8) not saving
  0098'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0H		;   the real UPDMARK maintaining them (below), no
  009B'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC		;   bias is needed: at cold OUTPOS=0 and UPDMARK
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-3


  009E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SRCREC		;   lowers it on an edit; PAGEOUT raises it.
  00A1'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKREC
  00A4'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKPOS
  00A7'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTPOS
  00AA'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTHI		; (appended) name.$$$ holds no record yet
  00AD'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TOPLF		; (appended) no line is behind the window yet
  00B0'   2B                    	DCX	H		; DEVIATION 8: the source holds all of it
  00B1'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SAMREC
  00B4'   CD 0418'              	CALL	FILLBUF		; WM 518 -- read the file into the buffer
  00B7'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi ':w' saves and keeps editing.  WM has no such
                                ; command -- its 'H' (EDNEXT, WM 525-545) ends the edit and re-inits for the
                                ; next file.  REOPEN is that re-init applied to the same file, and SEEKTO
                                ; pages the saved text back in up to the cursor's old place, flushing and
                                ; refilling exactly as the save loop (SAVCLO) does.  Without this, the editor
                                ; kept running on the flushed buffer and closed/renamed FCBs after a ':w'.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;REOPEN -- after a save: re-open the file named at 005CH and load its start.
  00B8'                         REOPEN:
  00B8'   CD 07FB'              	CALL	CLSBAK		; WM 526 (EDNEXT)
  00BB'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BINIT		; WM L02F2 -- reset the gap pointers
                                ;OPENZ -- OPENFIL after WM's L02F2 clears (WM 369-376): the source FCB's input
                                ; flag, extent, record count and random record, and NEWFIL.  At start-up the
                                ; input flag (005BH) holds whatever the last program left there; a file that
                                ; is not found must not be read from.
  00BE'                         OPENZ:
  00BE'   AF                    	XRA	A
  00BF'   32 005B               	STA	5BH
  00C2'   32 0068               	STA	68H
  00C5'   32 006B               	STA	6BH
  00C8'   32 007D               	STA	7DH
  00CB'   32 0000*              	STA	NEWFIL
  00CE'   C3 0000'              	JMP	OPENFIL		; WM INIT: FCBs, stale-file deletes, open, fill
                                
                                ;SEEKTO -- DE = record, A = byte (0-127) of a file position: page forward
                                ;until that position is in the window.  HL = its logical offset (the end of
                                ;the text if the file is shorter).  OUTPOS*128 is TXTBEG's file position.
  00D1'                         SEEKTO:
  00D1'   32 0000*              	STA	SKBYT
  00D4'   EB                    	XCHG
  00D5'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SKREC
  00D8'                         SKLP:
  00D8'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  00DB'   EB                    	XCHG
  00DC'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SKREC
  00DF'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = records past TXTBEG's
  00E2'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  00E3'   FE 02                 	CPI	2H
  00E5'   D2 0106'              	JNC	SKMORE		; >= 200H records: not in the window
  00E8'   1F                    	RAR			; CY = bit 8 (H is 0 or 1)
  00E9'   7D                    	MOV	A,L
  00EA'   1F                    	RAR			; A = bits 8-1, CY = bit 0
  00EB'   57                    	MOV	D,A
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-4


  00EC'   3E 00                 	MVI	A,0
  00EE'   1F                    	RAR			; A = bit 0 << 7
  00EF'   5F                    	MOV	E,A
  00F0'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SKBYT
  00F3'   B3                    	ORA	E
  00F4'   5F                    	MOV	E,A		; DE = HL*128 + byte: the target offset
  00F5'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  00F6'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  00F9'   EB                    	XCHG
  00FA'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  00FD'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  0100'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE = text in the window
  0101'   E1                    	POP	H		; HL = target
  0102'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff length < target
  0105'   D0                    	RNC			; in the window
  0106'                         SKMORE:
  0106'   CD 0398'              	CALL	FLUSHTX		; WM 4850 (SAVCLO): write it all, refill
  0109'   CD 03FE'              	CALL	FILLBF2
  010C'   D2 00D8'              	JNC	SKLP
  010F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG		; no more input: the end of the text
  0112'   EB                    	XCHG
  0113'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  0116'   C3 0000*              	JMP	SUBHD
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): the text outside the window, read where it lies.
                                ; vi's search wraps round the file, and WM's find can only page the window
                                ; there and back again to look (CMD.MAC SCAN, issue #35).  This reads one
                                ; record of it into SECBUF with WM's own RDSEC and CLNSEC, through the FCB the
                                ; pager would have read it through, and puts that FCB's record word and its
                                ; has-data flag back after -- so the pager never knows.  Only the open extent
                                ; moves, and SETREC re-opens the right one on the pager's next transfer, as it
                                ; does after a REWIND.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;SCNREC -- HL = a record, A = which: 0 one above the window (0 to OUTPOS-1:
                                ;below SAMREC it is the source's own, and from there name.$$$'s, as RWNREC
                                ;has it), 1 one of VIBACKUP.$$$'s, 2 one of the source's below the window.
                                ;Cleaned as FILLBUF cleans what it reads; name.$$$'s is read raw, as REWIND
                                ;reads it.  A = the bytes of text in it.  CY = its stream ended in it (a ^Z)
                                ;or before it (there is no such record: A = 0).
  0119'                         SCNREC:
  0119'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE = the record
  011A'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BAKFCB
  011D'   3D                    	DCR	A
  011E'   CA 013B'              	JZ	SCNCLN		; 1: the backup stack
  0121'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SRCFCB
  0124'   F2 013B'              	JP	SCNCLN		; 2: the source below
  0127'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC		; 0: above
  012A'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff the record < SAMREC
  012D'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SRCFCB
  0130'   DA 013B'              	JC	SCNCLN
  0133'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,OUTFCB
  0136'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0		; name.$$$'s: raw
  0138'   C3 013D'              	JMP	SCNGO
  013B'                         SCNCLN:
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-5


  013B'   06 01                 	MVI	B,1
  013D'                         SCNGO:				; HL = the FCB, DE = the record, B = 1 to clean
  013D'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  013E'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  013F'   2B                    	DCX	H
  0140'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  0141'   32 0000*              	STA	SCNFLG		; its has-data flag: an EOF or a ^Z clears it
  0144'   01 0023               	LXI	B,23H
  0147'   09                    	DAD	B		; FCB+22H, its record word
  0148'   4E                    	MOV	C,M
  0149'   73                    	MOV	M,E
  014A'   23                    	INX	H
  014B'   46                    	MOV	B,M
  014C'   72                    	MOV	M,D
  014D'   60                    	MOV	H,B
  014E'   69                    	MOV	L,C
  014F'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCNOLD		; the record word as the pager left it
  0152'   D1                    	POP	D		; DE = the FCB
  0153'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SECBUF
  0156'   CD 0898'              	CALL	RDSEC		; CY: there is no such record (A = 0)
  0159'   C1                    	POP	B
  015A'   DA 016A'              	JC	SCNEND
  015D'   3E 80                 	MVI	A,80H
  015F'   05                    	DCR	B
  0160'   C2 016A'              	JNZ	SCNEND		; raw: all of it, NC
  0163'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SECBUF
  0166'   CD 045E'              	CALL	CLNSEC		; CY: all of it; NC: a ^Z, A = the bytes before
  0169'   3F                    	CMC
  016A'                         SCNEND:
  016A'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  016B'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SCNFLG
  016E'   EB                    	XCHG			; HL = the FCB
  016F'   2B                    	DCX	H
  0170'   77                    	MOV	M,A
  0171'   11 0023               	LXI	D,23H
  0174'   19                    	DAD	D
  0175'   EB                    	XCHG
  0176'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCNOLD
  0179'   EB                    	XCHG
  017A'   73                    	MOV	M,E
  017B'   23                    	INX	H
  017C'   72                    	MOV	M,D
  017D'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  017E'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi writes the text to a name of its own (:w name,
                                ; and a buffer that has no name) and drops it for another file (:e).  WM always
                                ; writes back to the file it read.  These use WM's own primitives: SAVCLO for
                                ; the flush, RENAME for the backup, RENF, DELF, MAKEF, OPENF, CLOSEF.
                                ; TFCB holds the target name; the vi layer fills its drive, name and type
                                ; (bytes 0-11) and zeroes the rest.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;TEXIST -- Z iff no file has TFCB's name.
  017F'                         TEXIST:
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-6


  017F'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  0182'   CD 07D0'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  0185'   11                    	DB	11H		; search for the first match
  0186'   3C                    	INR	A
  0187'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;WRTO -- write the whole text to the file named in TFCB (the edit is flushed
                                ; to name.$$$, as WM's ENDEDIT does).  A <> 0: a file already there becomes
                                ; name.BAK (WM ENDEDIT); A = 0: it is deleted (vim overwrites it).  Then
                                ; name.$$$ takes TFCB's name, by RENF on its own drive or by a copy to another
                                ; drive.  REOPEN must follow (from TFCB's name).
  0188'                         WRTO:
  0188'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  0189'   CD 04EF'              	CALL	SAVCLO		; WM 558 (ENDEDIT)
  018C'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  018F'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  0190'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0191'   CA 01BE'              	JZ	WRDEL
  0194'   21 0009*              	LXI	H,TFCB+9	; delete any old name.BAK
  0197'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,WRTYP
  019A'   CD 0887'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  019D'   11 0009*              	LXI	D,TFCB+9
  01A0'   CD 0884'              	CALL	CPYBAK
  01A3'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  01A6'   CD 081E'              	CALL	DELF
  01A9'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,WRTYP
  01AC'   11 0009*              	LXI	D,TFCB+9
  01AF'   CD 0887'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  01B2'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB		; name -> name.BAK (WM 562)
  01B5'   21 09AF'              	LXI	H,BAKEXT
  01B8'   CD 0848'              	CALL	RENAME
  01BB'   C3 01C1'              	JMP	WRMOV
  01BE'                         WRDEL:
  01BE'   CD 081E'              	CALL	DELF
  01C1'                         WRMOV:
  01C1'   3A 0000*              	LDA	OUTFCB
  01C4'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TFCB
  01C7'   BE                    	CMP	M
  01C8'   C2 01ED'              	JNZ	WRCPY		; another drive
  01CB'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,OUTFCB	; RENF block: name.$$$, then TFCB's name
  01CE'   11 0010*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB+10H
  01D1'   01 0010               	LXI	B,10H
  01D4'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  01D7'   21 0001*              	LXI	H,TFCB+1
  01DA'   11 0011*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB+11H
  01DD'   01 000B               	LXI	B,0BH
  01E0'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  01E3'   AF                    	XRA	A
  01E4'   32 0010*              	STA	OUTFCB+10H	; the new name's drive byte is 0 (as RENAME)
  01E7'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  01EA'   C3 0867'              	JMP	RENF		; WM 566
  01ED'                         WRCPY:				; name.$$$ copied record by record
  01ED'   AF                    	XRA	A		; extent 0, record 0 on both
  01EE'   32 000C*              	STA	OUTFCB+0CH
  01F1'   32 0020*              	STA	OUTFCB+20H
  01F4'   32 0020*              	STA	TFCB+20H
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-7


  01F7'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  01FA'   CD 07EA'              	CALL	OPENF
  01FD'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  0200'   CD 082A'              	CALL	DELRST		; make the new file
  0203'                         WRCLP:
  0203'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0206'   CD 07D0'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  0209'   14                    	DB	14H		; read the next record
  020A'   B7                    	ORA	A
  020B'   C2 021C'              	JNZ	WRCEND
  020E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  0211'   CD 07D0'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  0214'   15                    	DB	15H		; write it
  0215'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0216'   CA 0203'              	JZ	WRCLP
  0219'   C3 08E6'              	JMP	DSKERR
  021C'                         WRCEND:
  021C'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  021F'   CD 0805'              	CALL	CLOSEF
  0222'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0225'   C3 081E'              	JMP	DELF
                                
                                ;DISCRD -- drop the edit: delete name.$$$ and VIBACKUP$$$ (WM EDEND, 581).
                                ;DEVIATION (not WordMaster): both are skipped when this session never wrote a
                                ;work record at all (WRKMAD clear), because then neither file can exist.  A BDOS
                                ;delete scans the whole directory whether or not the name is on it -- the best
                                ;part of a second each on a large drive -- and ':q' on a text that never spilled
                                ;paid it twice for nothing.  The per-file [FCB-2]/[FCB-1] flags will NOT do:
                                ;reading the backup back to its end clears them while the file is still there,
                                ;which is why WM's EDEND deletes unconditionally.
  0228'                         DISCRD:
  0228'   3A 0000*              	LDA	WRKMAD
  022B'   B7                    	ORA	A
  022C'   C8                    	RZ			; no work file was ever made: nothing to drop
  022D'   AF                    	XRA	A
  022E'   32 0000*              	STA	WRKMAD		; the deletes below leave nothing to drop again
  0231'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0234'   CD 081E'              	CALL	DELF
  0237'   C3 0818'              	JMP	KILLBAK
                                
                                ;CNTLF -- HL = the line feeds before the cursor: TOPLF for the records behind
                                ;the window, plus a scan of the text from TXTBEG to the gap.  It reads no disk.
  023A'                         CNTLF:
  023A'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TOPLF
  023D'   22 0000*              	SHLD	CLCNT
  0240'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  0243'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0244'   EB                    	XCHG
  0245'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPBEG
  0248'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  024B'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE = the text before the gap
  024C'   E1                    	POP	H
  024D'   CD 0289'              	CALL	CLBYTS
  0250'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	CLCNT
  0253'   C9                    	RET
                                
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-8


                                ;TLFADD / TLFSUB -- the sector at HL leaves the window's top (PAGEOUT) or comes
                                ;back to it (REWIND): TOPLF gains or loses its line feeds.  TOPLF is then the
                                ;line feeds in output records 0 to OUTPOS-1 at all times, which is what CNTLF
                                ;used to read those records back to find.  Keeps every register and the flags.
  0254'                         TLFADD:
  0254'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  0255'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0256'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0257'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0258'   CD 0277'              	CALL	TLFSEC
  025B'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TOPLF
  025E'   19                    	DAD	D
  025F'   C3 026F'              	JMP	TLFSTO
  0262'                         TLFSUB:
  0262'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  0263'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0264'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0265'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0266'   CD 0277'              	CALL	TLFSEC
  0269'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TOPLF
  026C'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  026F'                         TLFSTO:
  026F'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TOPLF
  0272'   E1                    	POP	H
  0273'   D1                    	POP	D
  0274'   C1                    	POP	B
  0275'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  0276'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;TLFSEC -- DE = the line feeds in the 128 bytes at HL.
  0277'                         TLFSEC:
  0277'   11 0000               	LXI	D,0
  027A'   06 80                 	MVI	B,80H
  027C'                         TLFLP:
  027C'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  027D'   23                    	INX	H
  027E'   FE 0A                 	CPI	0AH
  0280'   C2 0284'              	JNZ	TLFNX
  0283'   13                    	INX	D
  0284'                         TLFNX:
  0284'   05                    	DCR	B
  0285'   C2 027C'              	JNZ	TLFLP
  0288'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;CLBYTS -- HL = text, DE = its length: CLCNT += its line feeds.
  0289'                         CLBYTS:
  0289'   7A                    	MOV	A,D
  028A'   B3                    	ORA	E
  028B'   C8                    	RZ
  028C'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  028D'   23                    	INX	H
  028E'   1B                    	DCX	D
  028F'   FE 0A                 	CPI	0AH
  0291'   C2 0289'              	JNZ	CLBYTS
  0294'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0295'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	CLCNT
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-9


  0298'   23                    	INX	H
  0299'   22 0000*              	SHLD	CLCNT
  029C'   E1                    	POP	H
  029D'   C3 0289'              	JMP	CLBYTS
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; PAGING CONSTANTS -- WM 412-447.  From A/H = high byte of BUFEND, derive the
                                ; batch/margin sizing and the free-space water marks the load/spill path reads.
                                ;============================================================
  02A0'                         PGCONST:			; WM 412
  02A0'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  02A1'   B7                    	ORA	A
  02A2'   1F                    	RAR
  02A3'   1F                    	RAR
  02A4'   1F                    	RAR
  02A5'   3C                    	INR	A
  02A6'   3C                    	INR	A
  02A7'   E6 3C                 	ANI	3CH
  02A9'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  02AA'   32 0000*              	STA	PGSCAL
  02AD'   07                    	RLC
  02AE'   32 0000*              	STA	PGSCL2
  02B1'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  02B2'   FE 08                 	CPI	BS
  02B4'   D2 02B9'              	JNC	PGCON1
  02B7'   3E 08                 	MVI	A,BS
  02B9'                         PGCON1:				 ; WM 430
  02B9'   32 0000*              	STA	PGMARGN
  02BC'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  02BD'   FE 64                 	CPI	64H
  02BF'   21 0400               	LXI	H,400H
  02C2'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BUFLO
  02C5'   DA 02C9'              	JC	PGCON2
  02C8'   29                    	DAD	H
  02C9'                         PGCON2:				 ; WM 439
  02C9'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BUFHI
  02CC'   3E 08                 	MVI	A,BS
  02CE'   32 0000*              	STA	PGSCRA
  02D1'   DA 02D5'              	JC	PGCON3
  02D4'   87                    	ADD	A
  02D5'                         PGCON3:				 ; WM 446
  02D5'   32 0000*              	STA	IOBATCH
  02D8'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; SPILL / PAGEOUT / FLUSHTX -- the output (write-behind) side.  RAM-only, SPILL
                                ; no-ops (CKWRLIM) on load and FLUSHTX drains the whole buffer on save.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;SPILL -- WM 4386: write-behind a batch of TXTBEG-side sectors to OUTFCB.
  02D9'                         SPILL:				; WM 4386
  02D9'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  02DA'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  02DB'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  02DC'   CD 0308'              	CALL	PAGEOUT
  02DF'   DA 0000*              	JC	POPRET
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-10


  02E2'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SPLCNT
  02E5'   34                    	INR	M
  02E6'   46                    	MOV	B,M
  02E7'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,PGSCL2
  02EA'   AF                    	XRA	A
  02EB'                         SPLSUM:				 ; WM 4398
  02EB'   86                    	ADD	M
  02EC'   05                    	DCR	B
  02ED'   C2 02EB'              	JNZ	SPLSUM
  02F0'   3D                    	DCR	A
  02F1'   F6 07                 	ORI	7H
  02F3'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  02F4'   3A 0000*              	LDA	IOBATCH
  02F7'   3D                    	DCR	A
  02F8'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  02F9'                         SPLLP:				; WM 4409
  02F9'   CD 0308'              	CALL	PAGEOUT
  02FC'   05                    	DCR	B
  02FD'   CA 0304'              	JZ	SPLDON
  0300'   0D                    	DCR	C
  0301'   C2 02F9'              	JNZ	SPLLP
  0304'                         SPLDON:				 ; WM 4416
  0304'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0305'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;PAGEOUT -- WM 4439: spill one sector at TXTBEG to OUTFCB, bump TXTBEG.
                                ;DEVIATION 8: a record below SAMREC is the source's own and is not written;
                                ;OUTREC rises past it, so OUTREC still equals OUTPOS at every fresh write
                                ;(POFRSH adds one to OUTREC, not to OUTPOS).  OUTREC then means "valid in
                                ;name.$$$ or in the source".  While SAVCLO saves (SAVMOD), such a record IS
                                ;written, from RAM, and OUTREC is left alone.
  0308'                         PAGEOUT:			; WM 4439
  0308'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  030B'   CD 05E2'              	CALL	CKWRLIM
  030E'   D8                    	RC
  030F'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0310'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  0313'   EB                    	XCHG
  0314'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC		; DEVIATION 8
  0317'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < SAMREC
  031A'   DA 0363'              	JC	POSAME
  031D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  0320'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0323'   E1                    	POP	H
  0324'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0327'   D2 0330'              	JNC	POFRSH
  032A'   CD 091F'              	CALL	RECINC
  032D'   C3 034F'              	JMP	POADV
  0330'                         POFRSH:				 ; WM 4454 -- write a fresh output record
  0330'   CD 0919'              	CALL	WRRECP
  0333'   EB                    	XCHG
  0334'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  0337'   23                    	INX	H
  0338'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC
  033B'   D5                    POWHI:	PUSH	D		; (appended) OUTHI follows the most records
  033C'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTHI		;   name.$$$ has ever held; OUTREC cannot
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-11


  033F'   EB                    	XCHG			;   say, an edit behind it brings it down
  0340'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  0343'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0346'   D2 034C'              	JNC	POHI
  0349'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTHI
  034C'   D1                    POHI:	POP	D
  034D'   EB                    	XCHG
  034E'   04                    	INR	B
  034F'                         POADV:				; WM 4463 -- advance TXTBEG past the sector
  034F'   CD 0254'              	CALL	TLFADD		; (appended) its line feeds are behind the
                                				;   window now
  0352'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  0355'   19                    	DAD	D
  0356'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTBEG
  0359'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  035A'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	PGTOPM		; (appended) the window's top moved: 'u' reads
  035D'   23                    	INX	H		;   this to know its offsets have shifted
  035E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	PGTOPM
  0361'   E1                    	POP	H
  0362'   C9                    	RET
  0363'                         POSAME:				; DEVIATION 8: the source holds this record
  0363'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SAVMOD
  0366'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0367'   C2 038D'              	JNZ	POSAVE
  036A'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  036D'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < OUTREC: counted already, as
  0370'   DA 0383'              	JC	POSAM1		;   WM skips a record already written
  0373'   13                    	INX	D
  0374'   EB                    	XCHG
  0375'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC		; OUTREC = OUTPOS+1
  0378'   E1                    	POP	H
  0379'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  037C'   CD 091F'              	CALL	RECINC		; past it, unwritten -- and where WM would have
  037F'   04                    	INR	B		;   written it, SPILL's batch counts it as WM's
  0380'   C3 034F'              	JMP	POADV		;   does, so a first pass empties the window
  0383'   E1                    POSAM1:	POP	H
  0384'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0387'   CD 091F'              	CALL	RECINC
  038A'   C3 034F'              	JMP	POADV
  038D'   E1                    POSAVE:	POP	H		; saving: write it from RAM
  038E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0391'   CD 0919'              	CALL	WRRECP
  0394'   EB                    	XCHG
  0395'   C3 033B'              	JMP	POWHI
                                
                                ;FLUSHTX -- WM 4471: collapse the gap and PAGEOUT every remaining sector.
  0398'                         FLUSHTX:			; WM 4471
  0398'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0399'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  039A'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  039B'   21 0081               	LXI	H,81H
  039E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	WRLIM
  03A1'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  03A4'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTHOLE
  03A7'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  03AA'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTCUR
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-12


  03AD'                         FLXLP:				; WM 4482 -- flush loop
  03AD'   CD 0308'              	CALL	PAGEOUT
  03B0'   D2 03AD'              	JNC	FLXLP
  03B3'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;STAGSEC -- WM 4588: stage a short final record into SECBUF, ^Z-pad the tail.
  03B6'                         STAGSEC:			; WM 4588
  03B6'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  03B7'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  03B8'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SECBUF
  03BB'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  03BC'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  03BD'   0E 82                 	MVI	C,82H
  03BF'   04                    	INR	B
  03C0'   2B                    	DCX	H
  03C1'   1B                    	DCX	D
  03C2'                         STGCPY:				 ; WM 4599 -- copy the partial sector
  03C2'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  03C3'   12                    	STAX	D
  03C4'   23                    	INX	H
  03C5'   13                    	INX	D
  03C6'   0D                    	DCR	C
  03C7'   05                    	DCR	B
  03C8'   C2 03C2'              	JNZ	STGCPY
  03CB'                         STGPAD:				 ; WM 4608 -- pad the rest with ^Z
  03CB'   3E 1A                 	MVI	A,EOF
  03CD'   12                    	STAX	D
  03CE'   13                    	INX	D
  03CF'   0D                    	DCR	C
  03D0'   C2 03CB'              	JNZ	STGPAD
  03D3'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; FILLBUF / RDIN / CLNSEC -- the input (read) side.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;NEEDIN -- WM 4617: page input in when the forward read (RGET) runs dry.
                                ;SPILL first if free space is under a record, then reserve and fill.
  03D6'                         NEEDIN:				; WM 4617
  03D6'   CD 0479'              	CALL	INRDY
  03D9'   C8                    	RZ
  03DA'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  03DB'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  03DC'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  03DD'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BUFSUM
  03E0'   21 0080               	LXI	H,80H
  03E3'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  03E6'   EB                    	XCHG
  03E7'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFHI
  03EA'   D2 03F4'              	JNC	NDIRSV
  03ED'   CD 02D9'              	CALL	SPILL
  03F0'   DA 04B7'              	JC	MEMSHT
  03F3'   EB                    	XCHG
  03F4'                         NDIRSV:				 ; WM 4633 -- reserve free space, then fill
  03F4'   EB                    	XCHG
  03F5'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-13


  03F8'   CD 04AA'              	CALL	FREEREC
  03FB'   C3 0427'              	JMP	FILLRD
                                
                                ;FILLBF2 -- WM 4640: fill from input, capped at 7800H.
  03FE'                         FILLBF2:			; WM 4640
  03FE'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  03FF'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0400'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0401'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  0404'   11 7800               	LXI	D,7800H
  0407'   CD 04DB'              	CALL	BUFFREE
  040A'   CD 0479'              	CALL	INRDY
  040D'   CA 0442'              	JZ	FILRET
  0410'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  0411'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0412'   C2 0427'              	JNZ	FILLRD
  0415'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;FILLBUF -- WM 4659: top the window up from the input file(s).
  0418'                         FILLBUF:			; WM 4659
  0418'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0419'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  041A'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  041B'   CD 0479'              	CALL	INRDY
  041E'   CA 0442'              	JZ	FILRET
  0421'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  0424'   CD 0490'              	CALL	RESVBF0
  0427'                         FILLRD:				 ; WM 4668
  0427'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  042A'                         FILRLP:				 ; WM 4671 -- read & clean one input record
  042A'   CD 0445'              	CALL	RDIN
  042D'   D4 045E'              	CNC	CLNSEC
  0430'   D2 0437'              	JNC	FILRSV		; DEVIATION (WM bug): WM is JC L1C6B, which
  0433'   B7                    	ORA	A		;   skips the store for a full record (CY,
  0434'   CA 043A'              	JZ	FILRST		;   A=80H), so a file ending on a record
  0437'   32 0000*              FILRSV: STA	INLEN		;   boundary w/o ^Z leaves INLEN=0 and PAGEBOT
                                				;   RECDECs one record too far (record saved
                                				;   twice).  Skip only RDIN's no-record case
                                				;   (CY, A=0).
  043A'                         FILRST:				 ; WM 4677
  043A'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTEND
  043D'   0D                    	DCR	C
  043E'   C2 042A'              	JNZ	FILRLP
  0441'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0442'                         FILRET:				 ; WM 4683
  0442'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;RDIN -- WM 4689: read the next input record into [HL] (backup then source).
  0445'                         RDIN:				; WM 4689
  0445'   CD 099E'              	CALL	POLLBRK
  0448'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKRDY
  044B'   1A                    	LDAX	D
  044C'   13                    	INX	D
  044D'   B7                    	ORA	A
  044E'   37                    	STC
  044F'   C4 0894'              	CNZ	RDPREV
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-14


  0452'   D0                    	RNC
  0453'   11 005B               	LXI	D,5BH
  0456'   1A                    	LDAX	D
  0457'   13                    	INX	D
  0458'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0459'   37                    	STC
  045A'   C4 088D'              	CNZ	RDNEXT
  045D'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;CLNSEC -- WM 4709: mask bit 7, stop at ^Z; return live byte count in A.
  045E'                         CLNSEC:				; WM 4709
  045E'   06 80                 	MVI	B,80H
  0460'                         CLNLP:				; WM 4712
  0460'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  0461'   E6 7F                 	ANI	7FH
  0463'   77                    	MOV	M,A
  0464'   FE 1A                 	CPI	EOF
  0466'   CA 0472'              	JZ	CLNEOF
  0469'   23                    	INX	H
  046A'   05                    	DCR	B
  046B'   C2 0460'              	JNZ	CLNLP
  046E'   37                    	STC
  046F'   3E 80                 	MVI	A,80H
  0471'   C9                    	RET
  0472'                         CLNEOF:				 ; WM 4725 -- input EOF: return the byte count
  0472'   CD 08A9'              	CALL	IOEOF
  0475'   3E 80                 	MVI	A,80H
  0477'   90                    	SUB	B
  0478'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;INRDY -- WM 4733: NZ while any input data is still unread.
  0479'                         INRDY:				; WM 4733
  0479'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  047A'   3A 005B               	LDA	5BH
  047D'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BAKRDY
  0480'   B6                    	ORA	M
  0481'   37                    	STC
  0482'   E1                    	POP	H
  0483'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;MOREIN -- WM 4743: NZ if more input remains in the current direction
                                ;(WM's L26AA is OUTACT, the byte before OUTFCB).
  0484'                         MOREIN:				; WM 4743
  0484'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  0487'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0488'   3A 0000*              	LDA	OUTACT
  048B'   F4 0479'              	CP	INRDY
  048E'   B7                    	ORA	A
  048F'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; FREE-SPACE ACCOUNTING -- WM 4786-4841.  Reserve/compute the read-ahead room.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;RESVBF0/RESVBUF -- WM 4786/4790: reserve free buffer space up to BUFHI.
  0490'                         RESVBF0:			; WM 4786
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-15


  0490'   11 02D9'              	LXI	D,SPILL
  0493'                         RESVBUF:			; WM 4790
  0493'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0494'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFHI
  0497'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0498'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BUFSUM
  049B'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  049E'   E1                    	POP	H
  049F'   DC 04DA'              	CC	DISPKEY
  04A2'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFLO
  04A5'   29                    	DAD	H
  04A6'   24                    	INR	H
  04A7'   24                    	INR	H
  04A8'   EB                    	XCHG
  04A9'   E1                    	POP	H
  04AA'                         FREEREC:			; WM 4806 -- free bytes -> capped record count
  04AA'   CD 04DB'              	CALL	BUFFREE
  04AD'   FE 08                 	CPI	BS
  04AF'   DA 04B5'              	JC	FRECOK
  04B2'   D6 04                 	SUI	4H
  04B4'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  04B5'                         FRECOK:				 ; WM 4813
  04B5'   B7                    	ORA	A
  04B6'   C0                    	RNZ
  04B7'                         MEMSHT:				 ; WM 4817
  04B7'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMERR		; DEVIATION 7: out of room ends the key, not
                                				;   the editor (BUF.MAC's deviation 3)
  04BA'   4D 45 4D 20           	DB	'MEM SHORTAGE, TRY CLEARING QBUF',0H
  04BE'   53 48 4F 52           
  04C2'   54 41 47 45           
  04C6'   2C 20 54 52           
  04CA'   59 20 43 4C           
  04CE'   45 41 52 49           
  04D2'   4E 47 20 51           
  04D6'   42 55 46 00           
                                
                                ;DISPKEY -- WM 2846: PCHL trampoline (call the reserve routine held in HL).
  04DA'                         DISPKEY:			; WM 2846
  04DA'   E9                    	PCHL
                                
                                ;BUFFREE -- WM 4827: collapse the gap and report free bytes (A/C = pages).
  04DB'                         BUFFREE:			; WM 4827
  04DB'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTHOLE
  04DE'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  04DF'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BUFSUM
  04E2'   E1                    	POP	H
  04E3'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBCP2
  04E6'   EB                    	XCHG
  04E7'   29                    	DAD	H
  04E8'                         BFRLP:				; WM 4836
  04E8'   DA 04E8'              	JC	BFRLP
  04EB'   EB                    	XCHG
  04EC'   7A                    	MOV	A,D
  04ED'   4A                    	MOV	C,D
  04EE'   C9                    	RET
                                
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-16


                                ;============================================================
                                ; SAVCLO -- WM 4846: flush all buffered text to OUTFCB and close it.
                                ;============================================================
  04EF'                         SAVCLO:				; WM 4846
  04EF'   CD 0532'              	CALL	SVBEG		; DEVIATION 8: the source's front, counted
  04F2'   CD 03FE'              	CALL	FILLBF2
  04F5'                         SAVLP:				; WM 4849 -- flush all, refill, repeat
  04F5'   CD 0398'              	CALL	FLUSHTX
  04F8'   CD 054F'              	CALL	SVFRNT		; DEVIATION 8: ... and copied, the first time
  04FB'   CD 03FE'              	CALL	FILLBF2
  04FE'   D2 04F5'              	JNC	SAVLP
  0501'   AF                    	XRA	A		; DEVIATION 8: the pass is over
  0502'   32 0000*              	STA	SAVMOD
  0505'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TXTBEG
  0508'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PRSPAN
  050B'   CD 0000*              	CALL	LDHLI
  050E'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  050F'   CD 03B6'              	CALL	STAGSEC
  0512'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0515'   CD 0919'              	CALL	WRRECP
  0518'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS		; DEVIATION (not WM): WM closes here.  Text
  051B'   EB                    	XCHG			;   that was paged out, rewound and then cut
  051C'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTHI		;   short leaves the old records after the
  051F'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		;   last one, and CP/M cannot drop them.  A
  0522'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB	;   part-filled last record hides them behind
  0525'   D2 0805'              	JNC	CLOSEF		;   its ^Z padding; a full one has none, and
  0528'   AF                    	XRA	A		;   the old text was read back as the file's
  0529'   CD 03B6'              	CALL	STAGSEC		;   end.  So a record of ^Z goes over the
  052C'   CD 0919'              	CALL	WRRECP		;   first of them.  It is there already:
  052F'   C3 0805'              	JMP	CLOSEF		;   this write cannot fill the disk.
                                
                                ;SVBEG / SVFRNT -- DEVIATION 8: the records above the window that the source
                                ;still holds (0 to the lower of SAMREC and OUTPOS) are not in name.$$$.  SVBEG
                                ;counts them as the save begins (SVFCNT) and sets SAVMOD, so the save writes
                                ;the other records below SAMREC from RAM as it passes them; the records from
                                ;SAMREC to OUTPOS are in name.$$$ already.  SVFRNT, after the save's first
                                ;FLUSHTX has emptied the window, copies them from the source, bit 7 cleared
                                ;as a load clears it, through the free RAM above TXTEND: as many as it holds
                                ;are read, then written.  One record at a time, read and write alternate,
                                ;and the BIOS's deblocking makes each call about ten times dearer (0.37 s a
                                ;read, measured on the simulator's 8 MB drive).  The free RAM is at least the
                                ;0D80H a full register leaves.  OUTPOS, the save's place, is put back.
  0532'                         SVBEG:
  0532'   3E FF                 	MVI	A,0FFH
  0534'   32 0000*              	STA	SAVMOD
  0537'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  053A'   EB                    	XCHG
  053B'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC
  053E'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < SAMREC
  0541'   D2 0545'              	JNC	SVBN
  0544'   EB                    	XCHG
  0545'   22 0000*              SVBN:	SHLD	SVFCNT
  0548'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0H
  054B'   22 0022*              	SHLD	SRCFCB+22H
  054E'   C9                    	RET
  054F'                         SVFRNT:
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-17


  054F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SVFCNT
  0552'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  0553'   B5                    	ORA	L
  0554'   C8                    	RZ
  0555'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  0558'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0559'   2A 0022*              	LHLD	SRCFCB+22H	; the next record: OUTPOS keeps pace with it
  055C'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTPOS
  055F'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND	; all the free RAM above the text (FILLBF2's
  0562'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTHOLE		;   BUFFREE does the same next)
  0565'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  0568'   EB                    	XCHG
  0569'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFEND
  056C'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = the free bytes above the text
  056F'   29                    	DAD	H
  0570'   4C                    	MOV	C,H
  0571'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0H		; BC = the records they hold
  0573'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  0574'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0575'   C2 0588'              	JNZ	SVFFIT
  0578'   CD 07E7'              	CALL	FATAL		; cannot happen (see above): stop, never loop
  057B'   4D 45 4D 20           	DB	'MEM SHORTAGE',0H
  057F'   53 48 4F 52           
  0583'   54 41 47 45           
  0587'   00                    
  0588'   2A 0000*              SVFFIT:	LHLD	SVFCNT
  058B'   50                    	MOV	D,B
  058C'   59                    	MOV	E,C
  058D'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff they hold fewer than are left
  0590'   DA 0595'              	JC	SVFN
  0593'   44                    	MOV	B,H
  0594'   4D                    	MOV	C,L		; BC = this batch
  0595'   50                    SVFN:	MOV	D,B
  0596'   59                    	MOV	E,C
  0597'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = what is left after it
  059A'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SVFCNT
  059D'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  059E'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  05A1'   11 0000*              SVFRD:	LXI	D,SRCFCB
  05A4'   CD 088D'              	CALL	RDNEXT
  05A7'   D2 05B6'              	JNC	SVFOK
  05AA'   CD 07E7'              	CALL	FATAL		; the source ends early: never save half of it
  05AD'   52 45 41 44           	DB	'READ ERR',0H
  05B1'   20 45 52 52           
  05B5'   00                    
  05B6'   C5                    SVFOK:	PUSH	B
  05B7'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  05B8'   CD 045E'              	CALL	CLNSEC
  05BB'   E1                    	POP	H
  05BC'   C1                    	POP	B
  05BD'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  05C0'   19                    	DAD	D
  05C1'   0B                    	DCX	B
  05C2'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  05C3'   B1                    	ORA	C
  05C4'   C2 05A1'              	JNZ	SVFRD
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-18


  05C7'   C1                    	POP	B
  05C8'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  05CB'   11 0000*              SVFWR:	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  05CE'   CD 0919'              	CALL	WRRECP
  05D1'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  05D4'   19                    	DAD	D
  05D5'   0B                    	DCX	B
  05D6'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  05D7'   B1                    	ORA	C
  05D8'   C2 05CB'              	JNZ	SVFWR
  05DB'   E1                    	POP	H
  05DC'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTPOS
  05DF'   C3 054F'              	JMP	SVFRNT		; the next batch, if any
                                
                                ;CKWRLIM -- WM 4863: CY if GAPBEG is below the PAGEOUT write limit.
  05E2'                         CKWRLIM:			; WM 4863
  05E2'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  05E3'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	WRLIM
  05E6'   EB                    	XCHG
  05E7'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPBEG
  05EA'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  05ED'   EB                    	XCHG
  05EE'   E1                    	POP	H
  05EF'   C3 0000*              	JMP	CMP16
                                
                                ;CKRDLIM -- WM 4874: compare GAPEND against the read limit (PAGEBOT guard).
  05F2'                         CKRDLIM:			; WM 4874
  05F2'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  05F3'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	RDLIM
  05F6'   EB                    	XCHG
  05F7'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPEND
  05FA'   19                    	DAD	D
  05FB'   D1                    	POP	D
  05FC'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  05FF'   EB                    	XCHG
  0600'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; EVICTION SEAM + DEQUE MARKS.  Transcribed VERBATIM (WM 4335-4962).
                                ; MKGAP (BUF.MAC) reaches disk only here: MKROOM evicts a window edge (SPILL the
                                ; TXTBEG side to OUTFCB when scrolling forward, SPILLB the TXTEND side back to
                                ; the input/backup side when scrolling back).  UPDMARK keeps the three record
                                ; marks (OUTREC / SRCREC / BAKREC) that let PAGEOUT and PAGEBOT tell "already on
                                ; disk" from "must transfer", so nothing is written twice or lost.
                                ; PAGEDIR / PAGEWIN / PGNEED (scroll- and search-time paging) are real below:
                                ; PAGEDIR picks REWIND (backward, re-read spilled text) vs FILLBUF (forward),
                                ; and PGNEED / PAGEWIN keep PGMARGN bytes of text resident on the active edge.
                                ; The editor reaches them through BUF.MAC's PAGESTP and SCRLST (the line moves,
                                ; the line kill and the search sweep); PGBKTST drives PAGEDIR directly.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;PAGEDIR -- WM 4320: page more text into the window in the current scroll
                                ;direction -- REWIND (re-read text previously spilled to OUTFCB) when DIRFLG is
                                ;backward, else FILLBUF (read more of the input) when forward.
  0601'                         PAGEDIR:			; WM 4320
  0601'   CD 099E'              	CALL	POLLBRK
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-19


  0604'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  0607'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0608'   FA 06DA'              	JM	REWIND
  060B'   C3 0418'              	JMP	FILLBUF
                                
                                ;MKROOM -- WM 4335: free gap space by evicting a window edge (DIRFLG picks).
  060E'                         MKROOM:				; WM 4335
  060E'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  0611'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0612'   37                    	STC
  0613'   FC 064D'              	CM	SPILLB
  0616'   D0                    	RNC
  0617'   CD 02D9'              	CALL	SPILL
  061A'   D0                    	RNC
  061B'   C3 064D'              	JMP	SPILLB
                                
                                ;PAGEWIN -- WM 4350: keep PGMARGN bytes of text buffered around the cursor on
                                ;the active edge (for a whole-file search); PAGEDIR one increment at a time
                                ;until PGNEED is satisfied or the source runs out.
  061E'                         PAGEWIN:			; WM 4350
  061E'   CD 062E'              	CALL	PGNEED
  0621'   D8                    	RC
  0622'   CD 0601'              	CALL	PAGEDIR
  0625'   D8                    	RC
  0626'   CD 062E'              	CALL	PGNEED
  0629'   D4 0601'              	CNC	PAGEDIR
  062C'   B7                    	ORA	A
  062D'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;PGNEED -- WM 4361: CY if the active edge (TXTBEG scanning back, GAPEND scanning
                                ;forward) is still within PGMARGN*256 bytes -- i.e. the resident text on that
                                ;side is shorter than the margin, so more must be paged in.  LHLD MARGLO reads
                                ;the word whose high byte is PGMARGN and whose low byte (MARGLO) is a fixed 0,
                                ;yielding PGMARGN*256 (WM does this as LHLD 272F).
  062E'                         PGNEED:				; WM 4361
  062E'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  062F'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0630'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0631'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  0634'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0635'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TXTBEG
  0638'   FA 063E'              	JM	PGNCMP
  063B'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,GAPEND
  063E'                         PGNCMP:				 ; WM 4371 -- span the active edge, compare to margin
  063E'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	MARGLO
  0641'   EB                    	XCHG
  0642'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PRSPAN
  0645'   60                    	MOV	H,B
  0646'   69                    	MOV	L,C
  0647'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  064A'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;SPILLB -- WM 4491: evict a batch of bottom (TXTEND-side) sectors via PAGEBOT.
  064D'                         SPILLB:				; WM 4491
  064D'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  064E'   D5                    	PUSH	D
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-20


  064F'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0650'   CD 066D'              	CALL	PAGEBOT
  0653'   DA 0000*              	JC	POPRET
  0656'   3A 0000*              	LDA	IOBATCH
  0659'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  065A'   05                    	DCR	B
  065B'   87                    	ADD	A
  065C'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  065D'   0D                    	DCR	C
  065E'                         SPBLP:				; WM 4504 -- evict-batch loop
  065E'   CD 066D'              	CALL	PAGEBOT
  0661'   05                    	DCR	B
  0662'   CA 0669'              	JZ	SPBDON
  0665'   0D                    	DCR	C
  0666'   C2 065E'              	JNZ	SPBLP
  0669'                         SPBDON:				 ; WM 4511
  0669'   B7                    	ORA	A
  066A'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;PAGEBOT -- WM 4520: evict the window's bottom sector back to the input side.
                                ;If it still aligns with the original, un-read the source (RECDEC); otherwise
                                ;write it to VIBACKUP$$$ -- SRCREC/BAKREC decide which.  Then TXTEND -= 128.
  066D'                         PAGEBOT:			; WM 4520
  066D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  0670'   CD 0479'              	CALL	INRDY
  0673'   C2 0685'              	JNZ	PBSTEP
  0676'   3A 0000*              	LDA	INLEN
  0679'   57                    	MOV	D,A
  067A'   CD 07C5'              	CALL	SUBHA
  067D'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  067E'   7A                    	MOV	A,D
  067F'   CD 03B6'              	CALL	STAGSEC
  0682'   C3 068A'              	JMP	PBRDLM
  0685'                         PBSTEP:				 ; WM 4532 -- step back one sector at TXTEND
  0685'   11 FF80               	LXI	D,0FF80H
  0688'   19                    	DAD	D
  0689'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  068A'                         PBRDLM:				 ; WM 4537 -- check the read limit
  068A'   E3                    	XTHL
  068B'   CD 05F2'              	CALL	CKRDLIM
  068E'   E3                    	XTHL
  068F'   D2 0694'              	JNC	PBSRC
  0692'   E1                    	POP	H
  0693'   C9                    	RET
  0694'                         PBSRC:				; WM 4545 -- read from the source if its rec is due
  0694'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0695'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SRCREC
  0698'   EB                    	XCHG
  0699'   CD 07A6'              	CALL	RECBASE
  069C'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  069F'   E1                    	POP	H
  06A0'   D2 06AC'              	JNC	PBBAK
  06A3'   11 005C               	LXI	D,5CH
  06A6'   CD 0926'              	CALL	RECDEC
  06A9'   C3 06D1'              	JMP	PBFIN
  06AC'                         PBBAK:				; WM 4557 -- else read / recycle from the backup
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-21


  06AC'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06AD'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKREC
  06B0'   EB                    	XCHG
  06B1'   CD 07A6'              	CALL	RECBASE
  06B4'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  06B7'   E1                    	POP	H
  06B8'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKFCB
  06BB'   D2 06C4'              	JNC	PBWBAK
  06BE'   CD 091F'              	CALL	RECINC
  06C1'   C3 06D1'              	JMP	PBFIN
  06C4'                         PBWBAK:				 ; WM 4569 -- write back a backup record; step BAKREC
  06C4'   CD 0919'              	CALL	WRRECP
  06C7'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06C8'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKREC
  06CB'   2B                    	DCX	H
  06CC'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKREC
  06CF'   E1                    	POP	H
  06D0'   04                    	INR	B
  06D1'                         PBFIN:				; WM 4578 -- store new TXTEND; note input remaining
  06D1'   CD 0479'              	CALL	INRDY
  06D4'   B7                    	ORA	A
  06D5'   E1                    	POP	H
  06D6'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTEND
  06D9'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;REWIND -- WM 4755: scrolling back, re-read sectors previously spilled to
                                ;OUTFCB (by random record, stepping backward) and prepend them at TXTBEG.
                                ;Enabled only when OUTACT marks that text has actually been written out.
  06DA'                         REWIND:				; WM 4755
  06DA'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  06DB'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  06DC'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06DD'   3A 0000*              	LDA	OUTACT
  06E0'   B7                    	ORA	A
  06E1'   37                    	STC
  06E2'   CA 0715'              	JZ	RWNRET
  06E5'   11 064D'              	LXI	D,SPILLB
  06E8'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TXTBEG
  06EB'   CD 0493'              	CALL	RESVBUF
  06EE'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  06F1'                         RWNLP:				; WM 4768 -- re-read one output record backward
  06F1'   CD 099E'              	CALL	POLLBRK
  06F4'   11 FF80               	LXI	D,0FF80H
  06F7'   19                    	DAD	D
  06F8'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  06FB'   CD 0718'              	CALL	RWNREC		; DEVIATION 8: RDPREV, or from the source
  06FE'   DA 0714'              	JC	RWNDON
  0701'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTBEG
  0704'   CD 0262'              	CALL	TLFSUB		; (appended) its line feeds are back in the
                                				;   window
  0707'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0708'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	PGTOPM		; (appended) the window's top moved: 'u' reads
  070B'   23                    	INX	H		;   this to know its offsets have shifted
  070C'   22 0000*              	SHLD	PGTOPM
  070F'   E1                    	POP	H
  0710'   0D                    	DCR	C
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-22


  0711'   C2 06F1'              	JNZ	RWNLP
  0714'                         RWNDON:				 ; WM 4779
  0714'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0715'                         RWNRET:				 ; WM 4782
  0715'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;RWNREC -- DEVIATION 8: RDPREV on OUTFCB (DE), except that a record below
                                ;SAMREC is the source's own, never written to name.$$$: it is read from the
                                ;source through SRCFCB and cleaned as FILLBUF cleans it.  HL = where.
  0718'                         RWNREC:
  0718'   CD 0926'              	CALL	RECDEC		; OUTPOS - 1
  071B'   D8                    	RC
  071C'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  071D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  0720'   EB                    	XCHG
  0721'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC
  0724'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < SAMREC
  0727'   EB                    	XCHG
  0728'   D2 0740'              	JNC	RWNOUT
  072B'   22 0022*              	SHLD	SRCFCB+22H
  072E'   E1                    	POP	H
  072F'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCFCB
  0732'   CD 0898'              	CALL	RDSEC
  0735'   D8                    	RC
  0736'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0737'   CD 045E'              	CALL	CLNSEC		; bit 7 off
  073A'   E1                    	POP	H
  073B'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  073E'   B7                    	ORA	A
  073F'   C9                    	RET
  0740'   E1                    RWNOUT:	POP	H
  0741'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0744'   C3 0898'              	JMP	RDSEC
                                
                                ;MARKGB -- WM 4886: UPDMARK only when HL points at GAPBEG (falls into UPDMARK).
  0747'                         MARKGB:				; WM 4886
  0747'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0748'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,GAPBEG
  074B'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  074E'   D1                    	POP	D
  074F'   C0                    	RNZ
                                ;UPDMARK -- WM 4898: after an edit, move the record marks that say which
                                ;records must be written again.  Each mark only ever moves one way here:
                                ;  OUTREC (TXTBEG/output side) is LOWERED to OUTPOS + the whole records from
                                ;  TXTBEG to GAPBEG, when that is lower (stored on CMP16's carry).  UPDMARK
                                ;  never raises it; only PAGEOUT (POFRSH) does.
                                ;  SRCREC and BAKREC (GAPEND/input side) are RAISED to RECBASE less the whole
                                ;  records from GAPEND to TXTEND, when that is not lower (stored on no carry).
                                ;CMP16 sets carry when DE < HL.  (The comment here used to say the opposite
                                ;for both sides -- issue #37.)
  0750'                         UPDMARK:			; WM 4898
  0750'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0751'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0752'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0753'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  0754'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TXTBEG
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-23


  0757'   CD 07B7'              	CALL	PTRREC
  075A'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  075D'   19                    	DAD	D
  075E'   EB                    	XCHG
  075F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC		; DEVIATION 8: the source holds the text only
  0762'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		;   up to the edit's record
  0765'   D2 076D'              	JNC	UMKSAM
  0768'   EB                    	XCHG
  0769'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SAMREC
  076C'   EB                    	XCHG
  076D'                         UMKSAM:
  076D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  0770'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0773'   EB                    	XCHG
  0774'   D2 077A'              	JNC	UMKGAP
  0777'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC
  077A'                         UMKGAP:				 ; WM 4914 -- update the GAPEND-side marks
  077A'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,GAPEND
  077D'   CD 07B7'              	CALL	PTRREC
  0780'   CD 07A6'              	CALL	RECBASE
  0783'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  0786'   EB                    	XCHG
  0787'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SRCREC
